From 38021b3758c75f413a3bf5e899a65cf8b5221d92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dean Harmon <deannetharmon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:08:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Positions Strategy Filter (CSP, CC, PMCC, LEAP, BPS, BCS,
 IC)

Adds a multi-select strategy filter bar above the flat Positions list on the
Portfolio page, defaulting to all seven strategies selected.

resolvePositionStrategyFilterKey(pos) classifies each position into one of the seven
filter keys:
  - CSP, CC, PMCC, LEAP resolve from classifyPositionLifecycle()'s lifecycle-level
    classification (LEAP relies on the just-shipped LEAPS lifecycle type).
  - BPS, BCS, IC resolve from pos.strategy, since classifyPositionLifecycle only tags
    those as the generic SPREAD bucket and doesn't distinguish among them.
  - A position matching none of the seven (ASSIGNED_STOCK, a naked single-leg PUT/CALL,
    UNKNOWN) resolves to null and is ALWAYS shown regardless of filter state -- none of
    the seven chips claims to cover it, so filtering never silently hides an
    unclassified position.

PositionStrategyFilterBar renders the seven toggleable chips; filteredPositions (a
useMemo over the existing  array) is what actually gets passed to
PositionSection. PortfolioGreeksDashboard and PendingOrdersSection are deliberately
NOT filtered -- portfolio-wide Greeks and pending orders aren't in scope for a
strategy-specific view.

8 new tests for the classifier covering all seven keys plus the always-shown null case.
Verified: existing PortfolioPage.test.tsx suite (13 tests) still passes unmodified,
typecheck shows the same 41 pre-existing baseline errors, zero new.
